  "dom_id": "step-q78242",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "A linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation.  Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}48 \\\\ -32\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$",
  "worked_solution": "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}48 \\\\ -32\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =16\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =16v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=16v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=16.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}16 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 16\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
